---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.groupPages
  size: 1
  alias: group
  addAllPagesToCollections: false
navView: home
permalink: "{{ group.urls.home }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ group.label | capitalize }}"
  description: "{{ group.description | safe if group.description else '' }}"
---
{#- A group's landing page (2026-11-03), one per group with a subject, tab
    or not, at the bare /<group>/. Flat: one scroll, no second menu beyond
    the views row — the same idea as a subject page one level up. The group
    says who it is, shows its taste in one strip, names its subjects when
    there's no shelf to find them on, then everything written about it,
    newest first. Every band hides until it has something in it. -#}
{%- from "cards.njk" import tile %}
<article class="tag group-page">
  <header class="tag-head group-head">
    <h1>{% if group.hasIcon %}<span class="mico m-{{ group.id }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}{{ group.label }}</h1>
    {% if group.description %}<p class="tag-desc">{{ group.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  </header>

  {#- The card band: one strip, the group's "here's my taste" (see BAND_MAX
      in eleventy.config.js for what fills it). The CSS keeps it to the row
      that fits, so it never wraps into a shelf. The fuller views it stands
      for sit on its heading line — for a group in etc, whose views row is
      etc's, the only way to its canon and shelf. -#}
  {% if group.band or group.bandLinks | length %}
  <section class="group-band band-{{ group.band.kind if group.band else 'none' }}">
    <h2 class="band-head">
      {% if group.band %}<span class="band-title">{{ group.band.title }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% for l in group.bandLinks %}<a class="band-link" href="{{ l.url }}">{{ l.label }} →</a>{% endfor %}
    </h2>
    {% if group.band %}
    <ul class="shelf-grid band-strip{% if group.coverFit %} shelf-fit{% endif %}">
      {% for item in group.band.items %}
      {% if group.band.kind == "cards" %}
      {{ tile(item, ("/s/" + item.subject + "/#" + item.anchor) if item.subject else false) }}
      {% else %}
      <li class="shelf-item{% if item.canon %} is-canon{% elif item.rating and item.rating.slug == "favorite" %} is-favorite{% endif %}">
        <a href="/s/{{ item.slug }}/">
          <span class="shelf-card">
            <span class="shelf-art">
              {% if item.coverUrl %}
              <img class="shelf-cover{% if item.coverBox %} is-box{% endif %}" src="{{ item.coverUrl }}" alt="{{ item.title }} cover art" decoding="async">
              {% else %}
              <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ item.skyUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>
            {#- The canon strip says canon once per card, like /canon/; the
                shelf strip carries the shelf's two cells. -#}
            {% if group.band.kind == "canon" %}
            <span class="cell rating badge-g b-canon">canon</span>
            {% else %}
            <span class="cell badge b-{{ item.status }}">{{ item.status | statusWord(item.group) }}</span>
            {% if item.canon %}<span class="cell rating badge-g b-canon">canon</span>
            {% elif item.rating %}<span class="cell rating r-{{ item.rating.slug }}{% if item.rating.partial %} partial{% endif %}">{{ item.rating.title }}</span>
            {% else %}<span class="cell rating r-pending">pending</span>{% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          </span>
          <span class="shelf-caption">{{ item.title }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- Several subjects and no shelf to browse them on (sports' leagues): the
      subjects as a word row, busiest first. -#}
  {% if group.subjectRow | length %}
  <p class="group-subjects">{% for s in group.subjectRow %}<a href="/s/{{ s.slug }}/">{{ s.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
  {% endif %}

  {#- The log: every ## section about the group's subjects, newest first,
      each with its subject's cover in the art column; essays at their date,
      lede and link. The view pages' timeline, verbatim. -#}
  {% if group.stream | length %}
  <section class="timeline">
    {%- set entries = group.stream %}
    {% include "timeline.njk" %}
  </section>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">Nothing written yet.</p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
